<title>SOUTH KOREA: S.Korean stock market closed for Liberation Day.</title>
<headline>S.Korean stock market closed for Liberation Day.</headline>
<dateline>SEOUL 1997-08-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>The South Korean stock market is closed on Friday for Liberation Day. The market will reopen on Saturday.</p>
<p>The composite stock index ended 6.95 points lower at 755.78 on Thursday as institutional investors took profits following recent blue chip gains, brokers said.</p>
<p>They expected consolidation to continue on Saturday.</p>
<p>-- JEAN YOON (822) 727 5643</p>
</text>
